        rdfs:comment                   "Man's doublet, 1610-1615, English; Purple silk satin, brown silk woven lace trimming"@en , "Man’s doublet of purple silk satin, interlined with stiffened canvas, padded and quilted with wool and lined with beige silk taffeta.  It has a 2¼-inch (5.6 cm) standing collar decreasing to ½ inch (1.25 cm) at the front, 1-inch (2.5 cm) deep shoulder wings and curving 2-piece sleeves, with a high, pointed waist and 14 shallow laps.  Beige and brown silk woven lace, ⅜-inch (8 mm) wide, applied in parallel, covers the seams and decorates the collar, shoulder wings, sleeves and the laps.  The belly piece appears to be made of layers of linen stitched together and covered with beige silk. There are worked buttonholes down the left front, several missing, and 6 on each sleeve; no buttons remain.  The laps have 4 lacing holes, except for the 2 at centre front which each have 3.  There is a lacing loop of green silk ribbon inside each front above the waist. Two eyelets have been worked in each front above the waist seam on each side; each is threaded with a length of 1⅜-inch (5.9 cm) wide beige and purple silk ribbon to hold the belt."@en ;
